---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "13 August 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — LetsMock"
  description="The terms you agree to when using LetsMock, including subscriptions, refunds and the limits of AI-generated interview feedback."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-7 pt-18 pb-20">
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(34px,4vw,52px)] leading-[1.05] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.042em]">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="label mt-3 text-[11px] text-slate-500">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-10 leading-relaxed [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:tracking-[-0.028em] [&_h2]:text-ink-880 [&_p]:mt-3 [&_p]:text-slate-700 [&_li]:mt-2 [&_li]:text-slate-700 [&_ul]:mt-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_a]:text-violet-500 [&_a]:underline [&_a]:underline-offset-2"
    >
      <section
        class="rounded-[26px] border border-paper-300 bg-paper-100 p-7 [&_p]:text-ink-880"
      >
        <h2>Practice, not prediction</h2>
        <p>
          LetsMock is interview practice. The questions, scores and feedback are
          generated by an AI and can be wrong. Nothing here is a guarantee of
          how a real interview will go, and no employer is affiliated with or
          endorses this app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Using the app</h2>
        <p>
          You must be old enough to enter a contract where you live. Use
          LetsMock for your own interview preparation. Do not attempt to
          disrupt the service, work around usage limits, or resell access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. AI-generated feedback</h2>
        <p>
          Scores, "strong answer" suggestions and flagged weaknesses are produced
          by a language model. They are opinions generated from your transcript,
          not a professional assessment of your ability or employability. Speech
          recognition also makes mistakes, particularly with names and technical
          terms, so a transcript may not match exactly what you said.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Free tier and subscriptions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The free tier includes a limited number of interviews and a shorter time limit.</li>
          <li>
            Pro is a recurring subscription billed through Google Play. It renews
            automatically until cancelled.
          </li>
          <li>
            Cancel any time in Google Play. Cancelling stops future renewals; you
            keep Pro until the period you paid for ends.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Purchases are processed by Google Play and are subject to Google's
          refund policy. Requests are made through Google Play, not through us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Availability</h2>
        <p>
          LetsMock depends on third-party speech and language services and may be
          unavailable, interrupted or changed at any time. We do not promise
          uninterrupted service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Your content</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of your resume, your answers and your transcripts.
          You grant us only the permission needed to process them so the app can
          run the interview and produce your scorecard, as described in the
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the extent permitted by law, LetsMock is provided "as is" and we are
          not liable for indirect or consequential loss — including any outcome
          of a real interview or hiring decision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          <a href="mailto:hello@letsmock.com">hello@letsmock.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
